{"title":"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-pointed fork is a figure that consists of two parts: a handle that weighs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> \"skewers\" that each weigh a nonzero integer weight (in ounces). Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer such that there exists an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-pointed fork with weight <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/a/52ac5b064abbc3f58e265004e685ed103d1d3214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" />  What is the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Invites5.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/Invites5.png/400px-Invites5.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/Invites5.png/600px-Invites5.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/a0/Invites5.png/800px-Invites5.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If each skewer weights <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> ounces, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be a positive integer, then the total weight of our fork is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b313d2e45e5666aa0dd9a04a187f5700b49d2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+an.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" /> We equate this to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> and rearrange to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3d5cf92a41b35c47a28e5d0fcadb9cd579a9c68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12+an=n^2\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7c9621c584762ce732aa9d4562626af8f43e4a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[an=n^2-12\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb91ce24e6bb47d7433298836d1681ba699543bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=n-\\frac{12}{n}.\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a13ad17e62c5ebf4ac95ce37feaa2963d12ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> is not, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> will not be an integer. Thus, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, the only possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that yield an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b6b18612cb23307e22447a5a1e2218adae8445e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=1,2,3,4,6,12.\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"15\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is negative for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e67114e90e4c0f12e82962e548d38df58a5b4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> and so the only valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a615341e414d29defa5fdca62da315c685379c99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,6,12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> leading to an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fe1532cbd7c95b3fc64b9bd4203d58eb207e40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+6+12=\\boxed{22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"136\" height=\"25\" />. ~samrocksnature\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the integer weight is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />: we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1ca8be73e070090f2c81b480779ad88b7903bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-nk-12=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />. Now, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/1734911f2ca4a8010e21debff5753fb50c2dc6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12=2^2 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />, so we can have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/0814321ca9031fc29b82f86de21ff4a4dcfaeb83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-12)(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c4394e659dea0fbc640f5d69c7aa9866990627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-6)(n+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/893b24c6ae545fd69bb6f24cd62d6eb809aa4f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-4)(n+3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" /> to ensure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is positive. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/5604edd514ac47ec5083b380f4abdbc502daeb9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\{4,6,12 \\} \\implies 4+6+12=\\boxed{22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"292\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Geometry285\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the weight of each \"skewer\" is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> ounces. We then have that the total weight of the fork is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d140fe03dbf9309c03dd9630ea7ee62596dd5334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + nk$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />. This must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c58db4f9adba94a47735900dcf76c952168244fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 + nk = n^2 \\implies 12 = n^2 - nk = 12 \\implies n(n-k) = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"462\" height=\"21\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Also, the total weight must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces, so we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d523f0554830051a9999e876454bca330f6b2cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 &gt; 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. The factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> that have a square greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fe1532cbd7c95b3fc64b9bd4203d58eb207e40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+6+12=\\boxed{22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"136\" height=\"25\" />. \n</p><p>~Mathdreams\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015949\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 263/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8598/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.045      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    5.045      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21633:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015949 and revision id 158247. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}